From: immortalwrt-x86-fm350-pcie <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: gso: reject GSO_BY_FRAGS without frag_list

GSO_BY_FRAGS tells skb_segment() to consume segment lengths from
skb_shinfo(skb)->frag_list. A malformed UDP fraglist GSO skb can lose its
frag_list while keeping the sentinel gso_size value. skb_segment() then
dereferences a NULL list_skb in the segmentation loop.

Reject this invalid metadata before entering the segmentation loop. Valid
fraglist GSO and ordinary GSO paths are unchanged.

This is a defensive Linux 6.6 backport for malformed FM350 receive skbs.

---
 net/core/skbuff.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -4537,2 +4537,4 @@ struct sk_buff *skb_segment(struct sk_buff *head_skb,
 normal:
+	if (unlikely(mss == GSO_BY_FRAGS && !list_skb))
+		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
 	headroom = skb_headroom(head_skb);
